SUMMARY:[混合] Protest and Politics in Turkey in the 70s
LOCATION:Encina Commons\, Room 123
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/protest-and-politics-in-turkey-in-the
 -70s
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/protest-and-politics-in-turke
 y-in-the-70s\n線上資訊:\nRegister for Zoom link: https://app.smartshe
 et.com/b/form/019fafd2880c7c7f91ffa9589e8b28f0\n報名/票券: https://app
 .smartsheet.com/b/form/019fafd2880c7c7f91ffa9589e8b28f0\n\nProtest and Pol
 itics in Turkey in the 1970s: Echoes of Dissent offers the first comprehen
 sive academic study of Turkey’s protest cycle during the 1970s. Drawing 
 on an original dataset\, the book examines the interaction between collect
 ive action and state repression\, tracing the development of leftist\, nat
 ionalist\, and Islamist movements throughout the decade. The book also ana
 lyzes how the 1980 military coup suppressed organized political activity a
 nd reshaped the political arena\, contributing to the subsequent rise of p
 olitical Islam and the country’s broader rightward shift. By connecting 
 the political struggles of the 1970s to contemporary debates over authorit
 arianism\, democracy\, and protest\, the study contributes to scholarship 
 on social movements\, repression\, and political change.\n\nThis event is 
 co-sponsored by CDDRL's Program on Turkey and the Abbasi Program in Islami
 c Studies.\n\nABOUT THE SPEAKER\n\nSelin Bengi Gümrükçü teaches politi
 cal science at Rutgers University. She received her PhD from the Universit
 y of Zurich. She previously taught at İzmir University of Economics and h
 eld visiting positions at Bielefeld University\, Sciences Po\, Paris 8\, a
 nd the European University Institute. Her research focuses on social movem
 ents\, political parties\, the far right\, political violence\, and Europe
 anization\, with an emphasis on Turkey. Her first book\, Protest and Polit
 ics in Turkey in the 1970s: Echoes of Dissent\, was published by Routledge
  in 2026.
